<title>USA: Whitehall sets two-for-one stock split.</title>
<headline>Whitehall sets two-for-one stock split.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Whitehall Corp said Thursday its board of directors had declared a two-for-one stock split of its common stock in the form of a 100-percent stock dividend.  </p>
<p>The company said the split was pending approval of its shareholders of an increase in the number of shares from 5.0 million to 20 million at a February 17 meeting.</p>
<p>It said it would do the split on March 25.</p>
<p>In November, Whitehall reported it had 2.8 million shares at the end of its third quarter against 2.8 million a year ago.</p>
